  "limitations": [
    "This result establishes complete-checkpoint loading, repeatable output, and a controlled performance improvement, not Frontier certification.",
    "The paired runs fixed the GPU expert cache at 6,711 slots and KV capacity at 8,691 tokens. The prior KDA-FP8 evidence auto-sized 6,979 expert slots, so the 25.58% gain is intentionally calculated only against the new identical-geometry eager control.",
    "Fused FP32 mHC arithmetic changes reduction order relative to the eager path. Unit tests establish numerical equivalence, and two fused runs reproduced the same output hash and routes, but the eager and fused greedy hashes differ.",
    "The fused route selected 2.80 GiB more expert I/O than the eager control; the measured decode speedup therefore includes, rather than hides, that additional storage work.",
    "Route-first prefill still reads prompt-selected routed experts from NVMe; those compulsory cache misses dominate cold and warm TTFT.",
    "The host had pre-existing swap usage. The scoped run had zero swap growth and zero swap-out pages, but recorded 191 swap-in pages and therefore fails the strict memory gate.",
    "FlashInfer b12x cannot compile its fixed route-packing tile for 288 experts in the installed release, so the artifact uses FreeToken's Triton NVFP4 layout."
